 **Edge Cases:**
-- **Zero Points:** The method explicitly checks for `num_points == 0` and throws an exception [S1, unofficial].
-- **Precision:** Centering prevents loss of significance when coordinates are large, as the system is solved around the origin of the local sample cluster [S1, unofficial].
+- **Zero Points:** If `numPoints` is 0, the method throws an exception [S1, unofficial].
+- **Precision:** The centering technique specifically targets numerical stability issues in floating-point arithmetic when points are distant from the origin [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Subtopics
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-Not given in the sources.
+**Time Complexity:** Dominated by the SVD solve, typically $O(1)$ for fixed-size $3 \times 3$ systems, but depends on the number of SVD sweeps.
+**Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ auxiliary memory.
+**Strengths:** Improves numerical stability for ill-conditioned QEF systems [S1, unofficial].
+**Limitations:** Requires pre-computation of the centroid and matrix-vector multiplication overhead.
+**When to use:** When intersection points are far from the cell origin or when standard QEF solvers fail to converge due to precision loss.
 
